From: Sriram R <srirrama@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Sep 2025 10:48:21 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: guard non-transmit beacon setup during recovery

During an MLO group recovery, mac80211 can ask ath12k to restore a
non-transmitting BSS before its transmitting BSS has started. Passing that
invalid ordering to firmware can cause another firmware failure and leaves
beacon restoration stuck.

Reject the non-transmitting beacon setup until the transmitting vif is
started. Normal bring-up is unchanged because its transmitting vif is
already active.

Adapted from Qualcomm's downstream SSR recovery fix.

Signed-off-by: Sriram R <srirrama@qti.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Rajat Soni <rajson@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -1826,8 +1826,17 @@ static int ath12k_mac_setup_bcn_tmpl(str
 
 	tx_arvif = ath12k_mac_get_tx_arvif(arvif, link_conf);
 	if (tx_arvif) {
-		if (tx_arvif != arvif && arvif->is_up)
-			return 0;
+		if (tx_arvif != arvif) {
+			if (!tx_arvif->is_started) {
+				ath12k_warn(ab,
+					    "transmit vif is not started before non-transmit beacon setup for vdev %d\n",
+					    arvif->vdev_id);
+				return -EINVAL;
+			}
+
+			if (arvif->is_up)
+				return 0;
+		}
 
 		if (link_conf->ema_ap)
 			return ath12k_mac_setup_bcn_tmpl_ema(arvif, tx_arvif,
